ross us-east, us-west, eu-west). Actions taken: attempted rollback to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy, but it was rejected because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. Rolled checkout-api back to v2.2.9 (last healthy production release before v2.3.0) in all production regions; rollout reported VERIFIED. v2.3.1 is unhealthy and should not be redeployed until fixed. Note: v2.2.9 was the target because v2.3.0 is quarantined; please confirm v2.2.9 is not affected by CVE-2026-4417 and review whether v2.3.0 quarantine affects other plans.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 16937, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01VPep4gkMSqVYCP6Fpe7HmJ", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 16937, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01VPep4gkMSqVYCP6Fpe7HmJ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18626, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.2.9 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It is healthy again, with the error rate down from about 0.18 to 0.002.\n\nI didn't roll back to v2.3.0, which was the most recent healthy production release. The service rejected it because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. I then used v2.2.9, the previous healthy production release. The quarantine notice named only v2.3.0, so I didn't check whether v2.2.9 is affected by the CVE. Someone should confirm that.\n\nI opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It paged the on-call engineer and describes the failed v2.3.0 attempt, the v2.2.9 rollback, and the CVE question. v2.3.1 is unhealthy, so it should not be redeployed until it's fixed.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_012HbzfTb9U5MxTaH2ZsQSjT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01XQvMqyrAcMt7PbDKryWMVM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent production release that was healthy is v2.3.0. v2.3.1 is unhealthy in all three regions, and v2.3.1-rc was only in staging. Rolling back to v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_0147LYt2ki1N93rGk4T7vmwx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417, so the rollback was rejected and nothing changed. The next most recent version that was healthy in production is v2.2.9, so I'll try that.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Fru2n7ykd24iBXEcdRtpTD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.2.9"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Gh4jqq9jehpxPA9ucbTyuk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01VPep4gkMSqVYCP6Fpe7HmJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api rolled back to v2.2.9 after v2.3.1 health check failures", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api was failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate ~0.18 across us-east, us-west, eu-west). Actions taken: attempted rollback to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy, but it was rejected because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. Rolled checkout-api back to v2.2.9 (last healthy production release before v2.3.0) in all production regions; rollout reported VERIFIED. v2.3.1 is unhealthy and should not be redeployed until fixed. Note: v2.2.9 was the target because v2.3.0 is quarantined; please confirm v2.2.9 is not affected by CVE-2026-4417 and review whether v2.3.0 quarantine affects other plans.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.2.9 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It is healthy again, with the error rate down from about 0.18 to 0.002.\n\nI didn't roll back to v2.3.0, which was the most recent healthy production release. The service rejected it because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. I then used v2.2.9, the previous healthy production release. The quarantine notice named only v2.3.0, so I didn't check whether v2.2.9 is affected by the CVE. Someone should confirm that.\n\nI opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It paged the on-call engineer and describes the failed v2.3.0 attempt, the v2.2.9 rollback, and the CVE question. v2.3.1 is unhealthy, so it should not be redeployed until it's fixed.", "type": "text"}]}]}